      "message": "fix(pathkernel): a link can run outside the stock where the ground is proved\n\nThe link proof of the path kernel accepts a sample in the edge band:\noutside the stock, within one tool radius of a stock edge, as the entry\nstage's legal room defines it. The sample must not be inside the part\nzone (the part grown by the tool radius plus the stock to leave) and\nmust be more than a tool radius from each keep-out area. The stock\ninside the edge stays open only within the swath of a cut already made.\n\nThe region keeps the part zone of an Outside region, and the air leaves\nit out: a part that reaches out of the stock is no longer in the air.\nThe edge route can also walk along the loops of the air.\n\nPins: a link in the band over uncut stock (UNCUT_STOCK), near a\nkeep-out (HITS_FIXTURE), beside a part that reaches out of the stock\n(CUTS_PART, and no stay across it in the air), and a link out through\nthe air and back over cleared stock (stays). The K4 lift counts do not\nchange; the decision names the missing proof of each disc lift.\n\nRefs #4241\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
